customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayerCountCondition.Comparison.tooltip =  How the live player count is compared against the configured value.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayerCountCondition.Count.tooltip =  Number of players to compare against. Counts every player currently inside this volume, or every player across the group on group-level events.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.Source.tooltip =  Where to check for the tag: the tag event payload, this volume, the current group/spatial set, or a radius search.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.TagKey.tooltip =  Tag key required on the selected source, or the event tag key when Source is Event.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.TagValue.tooltip =  Optional tag value required under Tag Key. Blank matches any value for that key.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.Comparison.tooltip =  How the tag's value is compared against Tag Value. Exactly and Not Equal compare the text, and Not Equal still requires the tag key to be present. At Least, At Most, More Than and Less Than treat both values as numbers and never pass when either one is not a number.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.Inverted.tooltip =  Off (default): passes when the tag is present. On: inverts the check so it passes when the tag is absent.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.MatchKey.tooltip =  Used only when Source is Radius. Optional tag key used to choose candidate volumes. Blank includes every volume in the radius.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.MatchValue.tooltip =  Used only when Source is Radius. Optional value required under Match Tag Key. Blank matches any value for that key.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.Radius.tooltip =  Used only when Source is Radius. Maximum distance from the chosen center. 0 searches the entire world.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.Center.tooltip =  Used only when Source is Radius. Center position used for the radius search.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.MinimumCount.tooltip =  Used only when Source is Group or Radius. If greater than 0, this many candidate volumes must have Tag Key instead of requiring every candidate volume.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.BlockTypeCondition.BlockType.tooltip =  Block type assets to match. Matched against the block's base type, so stateful blocks still match when their base type is selected. Leave empty to match any block. Use the picker multiple times to add more than one.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.BlockTypeCondition.State.tooltip =  Match only when the block's state is one of these variants (e.g. Off, On, OpenDoorIn). Separate multiple states with commas to match any of them. Use default for the base state. Leave empty to match any state. Reads the live world block, so on a block-used event it reflects the state after the interaction. Press F7 in-game to inspect the state of the block you're looking at.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.EntityEffect.Effect.tooltip =  Entity effect asset to apply or remove.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.EntityEffect.Mode.tooltip =  Whether to add, remove, or toggle the entity effect.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.EntityEffect.Duration.tooltip =  Duration in seconds for temporary entity effects.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TriggerNpcMarkers.MarkerType.tooltip =  NPC marker type to trigger. Leave empty to trigger every manual marker found in the area.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TriggerNpcMarkers.Range.tooltip =  Extra search radius around each area volume's origin, in blocks. 0 only triggers markers that lie inside the volume shape; any value above 0 also triggers markers within this sphere.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TriggerNpcMarkers.MatchTag.tooltip =  Optional tag used to pick which volumes act as the search area. Empty uses this volume (or every member volume on group-level events).
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TriggerNpcMarkers.Radius.tooltip =  Filters Match Tag volumes to those within this distance of Center, in blocks. 0 includes every tagged volume in the world.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TriggerNpcMarkers.Center.tooltip =  What Radius is measured from: this trigger volume's origin or the triggering entity's position.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.ParticleSystem.tooltip =  Particle system asset to spawn.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Offset.tooltip =  Offset from the entity or volume position.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Anchor.tooltip =  Where the particle spawns: the volume center, the triggering entity, or the position the event/signal happened at.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Anchor.option.VOLUME.tooltip =  Spawn at the volume center plus Offset.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Anchor.option.ENTITY.tooltip =  Spawn at the triggering entity position plus Offset.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Anchor.option.EVENT.tooltip =  Spawn at the position the triggering event happened (a block event's block, otherwise the actor), or the origin carried by a received signal.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Scale.tooltip =  Visual scale multiplier. 1.0 is default.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Rotation.tooltip =  Yaw/pitch/roll in degrees applied to the particle system.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Duration.tooltip =  Auto-despawn after this many seconds. 0 lets the particle system run until it ends naturally.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SetWeather.Weather.tooltip =  Weather asset to apply.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SetWeather.PlayerOnly.tooltip =  Apply this weather only to the triggering player.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SetWeather.ResetWeather.tooltip =  Reset the weather instead of applying a new weather asset.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ShowEventTitle.PrimaryTitle.tooltip =  Main title text shown to the player. Insert a volume tag's value with {tagName} (using the tag's key). Unknown placeholders are left as written.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ShowEventTitle.SecondaryTitle.tooltip =  Subtitle text shown below the main title. Insert a volume tag's value with {tagName} (using the tag's key). Unknown placeholders are left as written.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ShowEventTitle.IsMajor.tooltip =  Use the major event title presentation.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ShowEventTitle.Icon.tooltip =  Optional icon asset shown with the title.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ShowEventTitle.Duration.tooltip =  Time in seconds the title remains visible.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ShowEventTitle.FadeInDuration.tooltip =  Fade-in duration in seconds.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ShowEventTitle.FadeOutDuration.tooltip =  Fade-out duration in seconds.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.PrefabList.tooltip =  Prefab list asset used to choose a random prefab.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Prefab.tooltip =  Specific prefab asset to paste.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Position.tooltip =  Position used when pasting the prefab.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.tooltip =  How Position is interpreted: an offset from the volume origin, the triggering entity, or where the event/signal happened, or an absolute world coordinate.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.option.VOLUME_ORIGIN.tooltip =  Add Position to the trigger volume origin.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.option.ENTITY.tooltip =  Add Position to the triggering entity position.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.option.EVENT.tooltip =  Add Position to where the triggering event happened, or the origin carried by a received signal.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.option.WORLD_ABSOLUTE.tooltip =  Treat Position as an absolute world coordinate.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Rotation.tooltip =  Yaw rotation applied to the pasted prefab. A trigger volume rotated on paste adds its rotation to this value.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.ShowParticles.tooltip =  Show block particles when the prefab is pasted.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.pastePrefab.preview.tooltip =  Toggle a world-space preview of the prefab at the trigger volume's location.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ControlDoors.Action.tooltip =  Door action to apply.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageEntity.Mode.tooltip =  Damage mode used for the triggering entity.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageEntity.Amount.tooltip =  Damage amount to apply.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.Mode.tooltip =  Kill runs the normal lethal-damage path (death animation and loot). Remove despawns entities silently. Players are never removed under Remove; use Kill to affect players.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.IncludeNpcs.tooltip =  Affect NPCs inside the volume. Narrow to specific roles with NPC Roles.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.IncludePlayers.tooltip =  Affect players inside the volume. Players are only removed by Kill. Remove skips them.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.IgnoreInvulnerability.tooltip =  Kill even invulnerable targets, including creative-mode players (like the /kill command). Off by default so builders in creative aren't killed while testing.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.Roles.tooltip =  NPC roles to affect. Leave empty to affect every NPC inside the volume.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.MaxCount.tooltip =  Maximum number of entities affected per activation. 0 removes or kills all of them.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoTick.ScheduledTick.tooltip =  Stop scheduled growth ticks inside the volume (crops and other timed plant growth). Growth resumes when the volume is removed or disabled.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoTick.RandomTick.tooltip =  Stop random ticks inside the volume (grass spread and other random block updates). Resumes when the volume is removed or disabled.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.CancelParticles.ParticleSystems.tooltip =  Particle systems to cancel. Leave empty to cancel any type. Only affects systems still playing that started inside the volume. It cannot stop systems that already finished or ambient effects the client spawns on its own.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.CancelParticles.Instant.tooltip =  On removes the particles immediately. Off lets them fade out naturally.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RunRootInteraction.RootInteraction.tooltip =  Root interaction asset to run on the triggering entity.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RunRootInteraction.InteractionType.tooltip =  Which interaction channel to start the chain under. This selects held-item/inventory context, cooldown grouping, and which chains can block or interrupt it - it doesn't check what the entity is currently doing.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RunRootInteraction.EquipSlot =  Equip Slot
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RunRootInteraction.EquipSlot.tooltip =  Armor slot index used only when Interaction Type is Equipped (0 = first armor slot).
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SetMusic.MusicContainer.tooltip =  Music container to force for the triggering player.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SetMusic.ClearMusic.tooltip =  Clear this player's forced music and resume world or ambience music.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.GiveItem.Item.tooltip =  Item asset to grant to the triggering player.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.GiveItem.Quantity.tooltip =  Number of items to grant. Values below 1 are ignored.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.GiveItem.OverflowBehavior.tooltip =  What to do when the player's inventory cannot fit the full quantity.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SetGameMode.GameMode.tooltip =  Game mode to set for the triggering player.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.ExceptBlocks.tooltip =  Block types this rule does not apply to, as comma-separated block ids. Leave empty for no exceptions.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoBuild.ExceptBlocks.tooltip =  Block types placement is allowed for, as comma-separated block ids. Filter blocks (reference blocks that stand for a whole family) are allowed and expand to their member blocks. Leave empty for no exceptions.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoUse.ExceptBlocks.tooltip =  Block ids that stay usable, as comma-separated ids. Also matches pickupable block/item entities placed with the entity tool by their item id. Filter blocks (reference blocks that stand for a whole family) are allowed and expand to their member blocks. Leave empty for no exceptions.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.ExceptBlockTags.tooltip =  Block tags this rule does not apply to, as comma-separated tag names. Any block carrying one of these tags is excepted.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.ExceptTools.tooltip =  Held items that bypass this rule, as comma-separated item ids. Leave empty for no exceptions.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.ExceptToolTags.tooltip =  Item tags that bypass this rule, as comma-separated tag names. Any held item carrying one of these tags is excepted.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.Target.tooltip =  Who receives the reject signal when this rule blocks an action. Self signals this rule's own volume, Other signals volumes matched by Match Tag Key within Radius of the blocked block, and Both does both. The signal carries the blocked block's position.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.SignalKeys.tooltip =  Comma-separated tag keys the reject signal carries when this rule blocks an action. Receivers match them with a Tag Condition (Source: Event / Signal), and the signal also carries the blocked block's position so effects fire at the denied spot. Paired by position with Reject Signal Values.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.SignalValues.tooltip =  Optional comma-separated value for each Reject Signal Key, paired by position. A receiving Tag Condition matches a key only when its Tag Value also matches (blank matches any). Leave an entry blank to send that key with no value.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.EntityFilter.tooltip =  Which entities this rule applies to: all entities, all except those listed in Entities, or only those listed.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.Entities.tooltip =  Comma-separated NPC role names (e.g. Trork_Warrior). Use Player to match players. Used by the All Except Listed and Only Listed entity filters.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDamage.PvpOnly.tooltip =  When on, only damage dealt by another player is cancelled, so PvE damage still applies.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.EntityFilter.option.ALL =  All
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.EntityFilter.option.EXCEPT =  All Except Listed
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.EntityFilter.option.ONLY =  Only Listed
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Multiplier.tooltip =  Damage is multiplied by this value. Above 1 increases damage, below 1 reduces it, 0 negates it.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Direction.tooltip =  Entity Filter / Entities pick the affected entity. The other party in the hit is not filtered. Received multiplies the damage that entity takes, so it is the victim and the attacker can be anyone. Dealt multiplies the damage that entity deals, so it is the attacker and the victim can be anyone. Both applies when the affected entity is on either side. With Entity Filter set to All, every entity in the volume is affected.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Direction.option.RECEIVED =  Received (affected entity is the victim)
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Direction.option.DEALT =  Dealt (affected entity is the attacker)
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Direction.option.BOTH =  Both (affected entity on either side)
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.EntityFilter.tooltip =  Picks the affected entity that Apply To refers to: the victim for Received, the attacker for Dealt, or either side for Both. The other party in the hit is not filtered. All affects every entity in the volume. Only Listed and All Except Listed narrow it to the Entities below.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Entities.tooltip =  Comma-separated NPC role names (e.g. Skeleton_Archer). Use Player for players. These are the affected entities for Only Listed and All Except Listed, and are ignored when Entity Filter is All.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoBuild.ExceptBlocks.placeholder =  e.g. Dirt, Stone
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoBuild.ExceptBlockTags.placeholder =  e.g. Soil
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDestroy.ExceptBlocks.placeholder =  e.g. Dirt, Stone
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDestroy.ExceptBlockTags.placeholder =  e.g. Soil
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDestroy.ExceptTools.placeholder =  e.g. Tool_Pickaxe_Iron
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDestroy.ExceptToolTags.placeholder =  e.g. Pickaxe
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoHarvest.ExceptBlocks.placeholder =  e.g. Dirt, Stone
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoHarvest.ExceptBlockTags.placeholder =  e.g. Soil
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoUse.ExceptBlocks.placeholder =  e.g. Door_Wood, Chest
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoUse.ExceptBlockTags.placeholder =  e.g. Door
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDamage.Entities.placeholder =  e.g. Player, Trork_Warrior
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Entities.placeholder =  e.g. Player, Kweebec_Elder
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.MatchKey.tooltip =  Tag key to match against. Leave blank to target this volume only.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.MatchValue.tooltip =  Optional value required under Match Tag Key. Blank matches any value for that key.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.Radius.tooltip =  Maximum distance from the chosen center. 0 searches the entire world.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.Center.tooltip =  Center position used for the radius search.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyRules.Active.tooltip =  Whether the matched volumes enforce their Always Active rules. Off suspends the rules at runtime without changing the configured rule list.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyRules.Operation.tooltip =  What to do to the matched volumes' Always Active rules. Set adds or replaces the chosen rule, Append merges the rule's list fields into an existing rule of that type, Set Field sets a single chosen field on an existing rule (empty value clears just that field), Remove deletes the rule, and Set Rules Active toggles whether the rules are enforced.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyRules.RuleField.tooltip =  Which field of the chosen rule to set. Leave the value empty to clear just that field. Other fields of the rule are left unchanged.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyRules.RuleType.tooltip =  Which Always Active rule this effect targets. For Set Rules Active, leave on All Rules to toggle every rule at once, or pick a rule type to enable/disable just that one.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.Enabled.tooltip =  Whether this rule is enforced. Turn off to suspend just this rule while leaving the rest of the volume's rules active.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyTags.Operation.tooltip =  How to change the tag on each matched volume. Set and Replace write Tag Value, Remove deletes the key when Tag Value is blank or only removes a matching value, Increment adds a positive or negative number, Toggle flips true/false, and Append adds Tag Value to the existing value.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyTags.TagKey.tooltip =  Tag key to modify on each matched volume.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyTags.TagValue.tooltip =  Value to write, add, or compare. Blank with Set or Replace stores Empty. Blank with Remove deletes the key regardless of its current value.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyTags.MatchKey.tooltip =  Optional tag key used to choose affected volumes. Blank affects this volume.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyTags.MatchValue.tooltip =  Optional value required under Match Tag Key. Blank matches any value for that key.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SendSignal.SignalKeys.tooltip =  Comma-separated tag keys carried by the signal. Receivers match them with a Tag Condition (Source: Event / Signal), firing if any key matches. The signal also carries the triggering event's position, so receiver effects can fire there. Paired by position with Signal Values.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SendSignal.SignalValues.tooltip =  Optional comma-separated value for each Signal Key, paired by position. A receiving Tag Condition matches only when its Tag Value also matches (blank matches any). Leave an entry blank to send that key with no value.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaceBlock.BlockType.tooltip =  Block type asset to place.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaceBlock.BlockState.tooltip =  Optional block state to apply to the placed block. Leave this field blank to use the default state.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaceBlock.Position.tooltip =  Position offset or absolute world position, depending on Origin.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaceBlock.Origin.tooltip =  How Position is interpreted.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaceBlock.ReplaceMode.tooltip =  Whether to replace any block or only place into air.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.FromBlockTypes.tooltip =  Block type assets to replace. Use the picker multiple times to add more than one.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.FromBlockState.tooltip =  Optional state that the source blocks must have. Leave this field blank to use the default state.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.ToBlockType.tooltip =  Block type asset to place when a matching block is found.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.ToBlockState.tooltip =  Optional block state to apply to replacement blocks. Leave this field blank to use the default state.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.Bounds.tooltip =  Whether to scan the exact volume shape or the configured AABB.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.X.tooltip =  AABB size along the X axis, starting from Offset.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.Y.tooltip =  AABB size along the Y axis, starting from Offset.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.Z.tooltip =  AABB size along the Z axis, starting from Offset.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.Offset.tooltip =  AABB minimum corner offset from the chosen Origin. Only applies to the AABB bounds mode.
customUI.triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.Origin.tooltip =  Where the AABB is anchored: the trigger volume origin, the triggering entity, where the event/signal happened, or an absolute world coordinate. Only applies to the AABB bounds mode. Shape always uses the volume.
